    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64553.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Yes, of course. There's a couple, actually. They've done pretty good work with respect to the Chinese Communist Party. I hope they'll lean in more. The fact they allowed this balloon to fly over the country was a mistake. But in terms of recognizing the threat, they have stayed consistent. And we flipped. 50 years of U.S. policy where it had been engaged, engaged, engaged. Trump administration, I led the charge, said, nope, that just doesn't work for the American people, for families here at home. And the Biden administration has kept that stance. They haven't come back to say these are just friendly competitors. They've now recognized the threat from the CCP.",
