    "turn_text": "Of course they did. And more importantly, there were actually people inside the United States government that didn't want this story told either, folks at NIH and elsewhere who wanted to tell a story that was different. I'll concede at the front end there wasn't as much certainty as there is today, but I was confident enough that in March of 20, three years ago, I went on ABC this week and said, that looks like this came from the Wuhan Institute of Virology. And I was called racist. You think of the names, unscientific Trump, MAGA, crazy. I would pick a term. It was because they refused to look at the data and the science. And so, yeah, the media dropped the ball. They're unlikely to admit that. They wanted to have a narrative that is different. I'll be honest, the Biden administration still won't say what needs to be said. That secure visor Sullivan goes out and says, there's not a consensus yet. There may not be a consensus and said, you're White House, but the whole world knows what really happened here. In 2019, they had a leak at the Wuhan Institute of Virology. It got out of the lab and Xi Jinping knew it. And when Xi Jinping learned that, instead of doing the right thing and getting the whole world to come in and help him solve this problem, he disappeared journalists. He covered up. He destroyed the evidence. And then he sent thousands of people from Wuhan around the world killing millions of people. That is said a serious business and the Biden administration's failure to acknowledge that to say, you know, we know what happened means one, it's more likely it'll happen again. That lab's still open, still operating as best I can tell the same way it was. And second, there's no tool to demand that the world holds Xi Jinping accountable for the lives that were lost and the impact it had on our",
