    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "It's hard to imagine the republic surviving for another 250 years. If you don't have voices in the media, they have the capacity to communicate broadly to the American people who are all trying to get the facts right. And they'll disagree. People will come to different conclusions. This is the story of American history from the Federalist Papers onward. So, no surprise, we have a rambunctious press. But boy, when they don't hold themselves accountable as well, when the New York Times tells you it's all the news that's fit to print and they narrate the Russia hoax for two years, printing that garbage that they knew at some point was false. And then don't say a darn thing about it and just take their pollsters and put them on their shelves. That's indecent. That's not journalism. That is political, polemic. And that is really dangerous.",
